      "page_title": "Partial Moves & Binding Modes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Partial Moves"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Destructuring an owned struct moves the bound fields out",
            "The original is then partially moved, unusable as a whole",
            "`_` does not move: `let Foo { a: _, b } = foo;` moves only `b`",
            "`let _ = foo;` drops immediately",
            "`let _x = foo;` holds it to the end of scope"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "The Constant Trap",
          "text": "`const MAX: u8 = 9; match n { MAX => .. }` compares. But `match n { max => .. }` binds — a lowercase name matches everything, and the compiler only warns that the later arms are now unreachable."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Binding Modes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Match ergonomics: `&Some(String)` vs `Some(s)` gives `s: &String`",
            "No `ref` needed since Rust 2021",
            "Matching `&mut` gives `&mut` bindings",
            "An explicit `&` in the pattern dereferences instead",
            "`match &v { &Some(n) => .. }` requires `T: Copy`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Landmines In Library Code",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`unwrap()` turns a caller's recoverable case into your panic",
            "Return `Result` and let them decide",
            "`if let Ok(_) = risky()` swallows the error whole",
            "Use `if let Err(e)` or `.expect()` so failure is visible"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Path",
            "What happens",
            "Cost"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Result`",
              "branch + move",
              "near zero"
            ],
            [
              "`panic!`",
              "unwind + drops",
              "orders slower"
            ],
            [
              "match",
              "discriminant + jump",
              "no dispatch"
            ],
            [
              "`Option<&T>`",
              "niche, no tag",
              "free"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Never Control Flow",
          "text": "A panic unwinds the stack and runs every destructor on the way. It is for broken invariants, not for the case where the file was simply missing."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Move Traps"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "match opt { Some(s) => .. } // consumes opt",
            "match &opt { Some(s) => .. }  // borrows",
            "opt.as_ref()  // Option<&T>",
            "opt.take()    // steal, leave None"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "\"use of partially moved value\" follows an owned destructure",
            "Bind by reference, or clone just the field you need"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
