        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Slice Arms Need Lengths",
          "text": "`[a, b]` matches exactly two. Cover the rest or the match is not exhaustive: `[] | [_] => ..` plus `[a, b, ..] => ..`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Type Mismatch Traps"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`map` where you meant `and_then` gives `Option<Option<T>>`",
            "`Some(Some(3))` vs `Some(3)` — the classic mismatch",
            "`if opt == Some(3)` compiles with `PartialEq`",
            "`if opt > 3` does not — the types differ",
            "`None::<T>` turbofish when inference has nothing to go on"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Honest Surprises"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Read Twice",
          "items": [
            "A match of all guards still demands one more arm",
            "That arm is not dead code — the checker is being honest",
            "A lowercase binding shadowing a const matches everything",
            "Fix with SCREAMING_CASE, or a guard `n if n == max`"
          ]
        },
        {
