    {
      "page_title": "Pipelines & The Ship Checklist",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Carry Forward",
          "items": [
            "`match` all, `if let` one, `let else` bind-or-bail, `while let` drain",
            "Exhaustiveness turns \"add a variant\" into a checklist — a stray `_` throws it away",
            "Niches make `Option<Box<T>>` free; fat variants cost every value, so box them",
            "`?` propagates and calls `From`, so error types compose up the stack",
            "Patterns are one language: `match`, `if let`, `let`, `for`, fn and closure params"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Before You Ship",
          "text": "No `unwrap` on user input. No bare `_` arm on an enum you own. Every propagated error picks up context via `map_err`."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Read on: The Rust Book ch. 6 and ch. 18",
            "`std::option` and `std::result` module docs",
            "The Rustonomicon on `repr` and layout"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Final Thought",
          "text": "Rust does not remove failure. It makes failure a value you must name — and then makes the compiler check that you named them all."
        }
      ]
