  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 2 of RUST SUM TYPES. Rust deleted null and exceptions, then handed the job to two enums and a keyword. This handbook walks the whole system: how enums are laid out in memory, why `Option<Box<T>>` costs zero bytes, and how match, if let and let else turn every added variant into a compiler-generated to-do list. 10 pages of dense field notes — save it before your next `cargo check`.",
